{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model using the advanced imagenet_vit_l image encoder instead of resnet50, maintaining pca_n2000 RNA encoding, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion. Validation accuracy of 0.629 (F1: 0.599) is slightly higher than the resnet50-based multimodal baseline (config_004: 0.6186) but remains lower than the RNA-only multiprofile baseline (config_003: 0.650). Uncertainty persists about whether the improved image encoder sufficiently compensates for the multimodal setup's inherent challenges and how fusion/encoding choices interact."
}

